{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardPart","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Pow","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Inv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Mul"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.energyPerArea_deriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.energyPerArea_deriv","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirEpsilonVacuum.lean#L59-L129","doc":"**Conditional Casimir-energy gradient** — §3b-cond conditional\ntheorem.  Given the plate-mode-count class, the derivative of\nthe energy per area is `π²/(240 d⁴)`; the force per area is\nminus this, i.e. `-π² ℏ c / (240 d⁴)` in dimensional units\n(textbook Casimir 1948).\n\n**Proof strategy.**  Elementary calculus on\n`f(x) = -π²/(720 x³) = -π²/720 · (x³)⁻¹`:\n\n1. `HasDerivAt (fun x => x^3) (3 d²) d`  via `hasDerivAt_pow 3 d`.\n2. `HasDerivAt (fun x => (x^3)⁻¹) (-(3 d²) / (d³)²) d` via\n   `HasDerivAt.inv` on (1).\n3. Multiply by `-π²/720` constant via `HasDerivAt.const_mul`.\n4. Use `EventuallyEq` (via the class axiom on `(0,∞)`) to\n   transfer the derivative back to `energyPerArea`.\n5. Simplify `(-π²/720) · (-(3 d²) / (d³)²) = π²/(240 d⁴)` by\n   `field_simp; ring`.\n\nThe `VacuumEpsilon` instance is not used by this proof but is\nlisted in the hypothesis to advertise the full §3b-cond\nconditional structure: both classes together are required to\n*interpret* this real-valued statement as the standard-part of\nthe surreal mechanism in\n[`conj:casimir-epsilon-vacuum`](../../../quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/casimir-epsilon-vacuum.md). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum.energyPerArea_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum.energyPerArea_eq","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirEpsilonVacuum.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Scaling axiom — the standard-physics result that the QOU\nderivation must reproduce.  Sign: negative (lower energy\nbetween plates than outside means the force is attractive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum.energyPerArea","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum.energyPerArea","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirEpsilonVacuum.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Archimedean energy per unit area between two parallel\nconducting plates separated by `d`, in units where\n`ℏc = 1`.  The conjecture is that this equals\n`-π²/(720 d³)` — the standard-physics Casimir result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirEpsilonVacuum.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirEpsilonVacuum","kind":"class","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirEpsilonVacuum.lean#L36-L57","doc":"**Plate-mode-count class** — §3b-cond axiomatisation of the\nsurreal-coefficient appearing in the parallel-plate Casimir\nconjecture.  See\n[`conj:casimir-epsilon-vacuum`](../../../quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/casimir-epsilon-vacuum.md).\n\nThe class carries the *archimedean image* of the surreal\nquantity `(N⊙^in − N⊙^out) · ε`.  The surreal `ε⁻¹` and `ε`\ncancel in the energy density `u(d) = ε·(N⊙^in − N⊙^out)/A`,\nleaving a real-valued function.  This class encodes that\nreal-valued energy-density function directly. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:casimir-epsilon-vacuum","label":"conj:casimir-epsilon-vacuum","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/casimir-epsilon-vacuum.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}